{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: inlined the construction of the regression coefficient vector in the likelihood so that `beta0` and `beta1` are not used in the model block before their prior sampling statements. The statistical model and likelihood are unchanged. `M`, `N`, `X`, and `x0` remain unprotected context data. `data_safe.json` is unchanged; no deterministic copies or reshapes were added.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] real y;      // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M + 1] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n, 1] = 1;
    deltaX[n, 2:(M + 1)] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real beta0;          // Intercept
  vector[M] beta1;     // Slopes
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement Variability
}

model {
  // Prior model
  beta0 ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta1 ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 5);

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ normal(deltaX * append_row(beta0, beta1), sigma);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  array[N] real y_pred = normal_rng(deltaX * append_row(beta0, beta1), sigma);
}
